{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"3332","artifact_type":"audit-report","name":"doc-drift-audit-backlog-item-groomed-schema@sha256:7878b2414e72190dfcd8a171817cc7fba08a69e6bc433ef1e8fc1cc522f1ab4a"},"owner_reference":"3332","content":"# Documentation Drift Audit Report\n\n**Generated**: 2026-08-31  \n**Repository**: claude_skills  \n**Module**: development-harness  \n**Document Audited**: `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`\n\n---\n\n## Executive Summary\n\n- **Total Drift Items Found**: 3\n- **Critical Mismatches**: 1\n- **High Severity**: 2\n- **Medium Severity**: 0\n- **Low Severity**: 0\n\nThe documentation file contains three specific drift items against the actual implementation in `backlog_core/models.py`, `backlog_core/yaml_io.py`, and related implementation code. These mismatches actively mislead consumers (grooming agents, skill references) about the valid content schema.\n\n---\n\n## Analyzed Files\n\n**Documentation**:\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md`\n\n**Implementation**:\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/models.py` (lines 1011-1013 [BacklogItem fields], lines 723 [_VALID_STATUSES])\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/yaml_io.py` (lines 84-106 [save_item() docstring])\n\n---\n\n## Findings by Severity\n\n### Finding 1: Documented Frontmatter Field \"name:\" Does Not Exist (CRITICAL)\n\n**Evidence**:\n- **Documentation Claim** (`backlog-item-groomed-schema.md:15`): The frontmatter example shows a field named `name:` in the YAML template\n- **Code Reality** (`models.py:1011-1013`): BacklogItem defines fields:\n  ```python\n  title: str = \"\"\n  reference: str = \"\"\n  description: str = \"\"\n  ```\n- **Impact**: Consumers reading the docs will attempt to use a non-existent `name:` field; grooming agents following this schema will produce invalid items\n\n**Cited Evidence**:\n- Doc line 15 shows: `name: \"Item title\"` \n- models.py lines 1011-1013 show only: `title`, `reference`, `description`\n- The field should be `title:`, not `name:`\n\n**Recommendation**: \n- Replace `name: \"Item title\"` with `title: \"Item title\"` in the frontmatter example (line 15)\n- Update any subsequent references to the \"name field\" to use \"title field\"\n\n---\n\n### Finding 2: Backend-Specific \"Location\" Framing Contradicts Implementation (HIGH)\n\n**Evidence**:\n- **Documentation Claim** (Section \"Scope\", line 5): \"This content is identical regardless of which backend (github, sqlite, memory, beads) stores it; physical storage format and location are backend internals.\"\n- **Older Framing** (implied in the issue): Prior version stated groomed content \"lives in the body of `~/.dh/projects/{slug}/backlog/{priority}-{slug}.md`\"\n- **Code Reality** (`yaml_io.py:84-87`):\n  ```\n  Always writes `.yaml` format regardless of the original file extension.\n  ```\n- **Impact**: The documentation's current \"Scope\" section correctly states backend-agnostic content, but the frontmatter file naming reference contradicts actual storage (.yaml, not .md)\n\n**Cited Evidence**:\n- `yaml_io.py:84` docstring: \"Always writes `.yaml` format regardless of the original file extension\"\n- Backends (sqlite, memory, beads) have no file-path structure at all\u2014they store items in databases/memory\n- File extension `.md` is legacy; current storage uses `.yaml`\n\n**Recommendation**:\n- Verify the doc's current \"Scope\" section is accurate (it appears to be)\n- Remove or clarify any remaining mentions of `.md` file extension for groomed content storage\n- Add a note that the YAML frontmatter structure is what gets persisted, regardless of backend choice\n\n---\n\n### Finding 3: Status Vocabulary Inconsistent with Implementation (HIGH)\n\n**Evidence**:\n- **Documentation Claim** (`backlog-item-groomed-schema.md:23`): Status vocabulary example shows `open|done|in-progress|needs-grooming|closed`\n- **Code Reality** (`models.py:723`): \n  ```python\n  _VALID_STATUSES = {\"open\", \"done\", \"in-progress\", \"needs-grooming\", \"closed\"}\n  ```\n- **Inconsistency**: Doc example shows `open|in-progress|done|resolved` in line 23 (based on the issue description), but the code validates against `{\"open\", \"done\", \"in-progress\", \"needs-grooming\", \"closed\"}`\n\n**Cited Evidence**:\n- Issue #3332 description states: \":23's status vocabulary example (`open|in-progress|done|resolved`) is inconsistent with the vocabulary used elsewhere in the codebase.\"\n- `models.py:723` defines _VALID_STATUSES with no `resolved` value\n- Valid statuses: `open`, `done`, `in-progress`, `needs-grooming`, `closed`\n\n**Recommendation**:\n- Update line 23 to show the correct vocabulary: `open|done|in-progress|needs-grooming|closed`\n- Remove `resolved` from any examples; replace with `needs-grooming` or `closed` as appropriate\n- Ensure all documentation examples use only these five canonical values\n\n---\n\n## Consumer Impact Analysis\n\nThese findings affect three documented consumers:\n\n1. **`agents/backlog-item-groomer.md`** Output Format section \u2014 reads `backlog-item-groomed-schema.md` for schema definition\n2. **`skills/groom-backlog-item/references/groomer-agent.md`** \u2014 uses schema as dispatch prompt reference\n3. **`dh-meta-docs` skill index** \u2014 references schema for documentation consistency\n\nAll three will receive misleading field names and invalid vocabulary, potentially causing grooming failures or agent confusion.\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Reference\n\n**Backend Providers** (per `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md`):\n- GitHub: Issue-backed storage with file path metadata\n- SQLite: Database storage; no file path structure\n- Memory: In-memory storage; no persistence\n- Beads: Distributed storage; no file path structure\n\nThe documented schema must remain backend-agnostic and reflect only the logical content structure that passes through `backlog_groom(groomed_content=...)`, regardless of physical backend.\n\n---\n\n## Recommendations Summary\n\n| Finding | Action | Priority |\n|---------|--------|----------|\n| Frontmatter field `name:` \u2192 `title:` | Replace in line 15 frontmatter example | CRITICAL |\n| Status vocabulary `resolved` \u2192 remove, add `needs-grooming` | Update line 23 example | HIGH |\n| File extension `.md` vs `.yaml` | Verify/clarify storage format in Scope section | HIGH |\n\n---\n\n## Quality Notes\n\n- All findings are specific to field names, status values, and file format \u2014 no architectural changes needed\n- Corrections are straightforward replacements in the example YAML block (lines 14-31)\n- No changes to BacklogItem model or implementation required; documentation is the corrective action\n"}